27
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.560
This exploit is wormable.

28
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.600
A single infected robot sitting in a
police storage room

29
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.960
will automatically scan for and compromise
any other unit that

30
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.280
wanders nearby. Deeper inside the code is
an undocumented remote

31
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.440
access tunnel. When active, this back door
bypasses the owner's

32
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.680
controls, deliberately sending encrypted
data from the robot straight to

33
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.400
servers operated by foreign tech giants.

34
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.480
Standard safety frameworks completely
missed a wormable exploit and a

35
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.320
hidden exfiltration channel.

36
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.400
They missed it because the auditors were
evaluating the wrong

37
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.240
layer of the technology.

38
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.080
This animation represents what researchers
call the goal layer.

39
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.520
You give the system a surface level
instruction, like patrol

40
00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.800
the perimeter, and you observe whether it
successfully completes the

41
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.240
physical task. If the machine walks the
loop without falling

42
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.360
over, a conventional safety auditor stamps
a pass on the

43
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.240
clipboard and calls the system compliant.

44
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.360
Below that surface instruction is the
process layer.

45
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.200
This is the underlying architecture
governing how the system deliberates,

46
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.400
executes commands, and routes its internal
data.

47
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.680
Process layer attacks are invisible to
standard audits.

48
00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.320
A robot can flawlessly execute a perimeter
patrol while simultaneously

49
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.400
running an unauthenticated middleware
exploit on a parallel path underneath

50
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.160
the primary command.

51
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.320
Because the physical behavior looks
normal, goal layer evaluations are

52
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.960
effectively useless for embodied AI.

53
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.880
They cannot detect when the underlying
logic of the machine

54
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.320
has been corrupted.

55
00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:57.160
That hidden data tunnel, the cloud sale
backdoor, is actively

56
00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.800
engineered to exploit this blind spot.

57
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.000
If the robot senses its network traffic is
being monitored,

58
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.280
it dynamically shifts its routing, hiding
