59
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.680
those foreign servers from the operator.

60
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.320
To block this data leak, a police
department has to

61
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.400
set up custom network monitors.

62
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.640
But to do that, they have to use the
robot's

63
00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.600
own broken firmware to gain root access
and overwrite the

64
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.800
factory settings. Once you route the
device to block the

65
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.800
backdoor, you can never install a vendor
security update again.

66
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.960
Doing so overrides the custom network
monitor and restores the

67
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.480
vendor's access. To stop the data leak,
you must leave

68
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.480
the robot permanently exposed to that
wormable Bluetooth exploit.

69
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.680
There is no structurally safe way to
operate these specific

70
00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.600
models. Fixing the hidden data leak
requires permanently enabling a

71
00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.880
